{{Episode list/sublist|Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D. season 5
| EpisodeNumber   = 92
| EpisodeNumber2  = 4
| Title           = A Life Earned
| DirectedBy      = [[Stanley Brooks|Stan Brooks]]
| WrittenBy       = [[Drew Z. Greenberg]]
| OriginalAirDate = {{Start date|2017|12|15}}
| Viewers         = 1.84<ref name="504Ratings">{{Cite web |last=Porter |first=Rick |date=December 18, 2017 |title='Hawaii Five-0' adjusts down: Friday final ratings |url=http://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/daily-ratings/friday-final-ratings-dec-15-2017/ |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171220175227/http://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/daily-ratings/friday-final-ratings-dec-15-2017/ |archive-date=December 20, 2017 |access-date=December 18, 2017 |website=[[TV by the Numbers]]}}</ref>
| ShortSummary    = Daisy meets [[Ben (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Ben]], one of Kasius' other champions, capable of [[telepathy]]. Using Ben to corroborate their story, Kasius interrogates Daisy and Simmons about the others. They are able to convince Kasius they came alone, though he remains suspicious. During the interrogation, Ben learns that Kasius intends to destroy the station and everyone on it once he acquires enough profits to leave. Deke returns to the others to gather new information as they learn about the mysterious Level 35. Recognizing his father's voice on the radio transmission, Deke agrees to help them gain access to the restricted floor. There, they discover that Kasius is attempting to breed Inhumans. May also discovers Deke lied about Daisy's whereabouts, but gets interrupted by [[Sinara (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Sinara]]. Coulson leaves with Deke while May fights Sinara alone. Meanwhile, Grill sends Mack to confront someone who owes him payment. Later, Fitz is revealed to be one of the bidders who has arrived for Daisy's exhibition.
| LineColor       = 322D39
}}
{{Episode list/sublist|Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D. season 5
| EpisodeNumber   = 93
| EpisodeNumber2  = 5
| Title           = Rewind
| DirectedBy      = Jesse Bochco
| WrittenBy       = [[Craig Titley]]
| OriginalAirDate = {{Start date|2017|12|22}}
| Viewers         = 2.40<ref name="505Ratings">{{Cite web |last=Porter |first=Rick |date=December 26, 2017 |title='Blindspot,' 'I Love Lucy' special and others unchanged: Friday final ratings |url=http://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/daily-ratings/friday-final-ratings-dec-22-2017/ |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171227121807/http://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/daily-ratings/friday-final-ratings-dec-22-2017/ |archive-date=December 27, 2017 |access-date=December 26, 2017 |website=[[TV by the Numbers]]}}</ref>
| ShortSummary    = Shortly after the others are taken from the diner, Fitz is taken into military custody and interrogated by [[General Hale]] and her subordinates about the others' whereabouts, as well as their involvement in the assassination attempt on General [[Glenn Talbot (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Glenn Talbot]]{{efn|As depicted in "[[World's End (Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D.)|World's End]]".}} and the deaths of [[Jeffrey Mace (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Jeffrey Mace]] and [[Holden Radcliffe (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Holden Radcliffe]]. For the next six months, Fitz is given special privileges to allow him to locate the team, but he fails. With help from [[Lance Hunter (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Lance Hunter]], Fitz escapes the military facility and tracks down [[Enoch (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Enoch]], the man who took the others. Enoch explains that a prophecy foretold these events and takes them to meet [[Robin Hinton|Robin]], the daughter of [[Charles Hinton (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Charles Hinton]] who expresses her prophetic abilities through drawings. Tracked by the military, Enoch helps them escape to a secret bunker where Fitz learns that he was left behind so he could save the team. Determined to help them, Fitz and Hunter break back into Hale's military facility to obtain a cryogenic pod; they find all their old S.H.I.E.L.D. tech, including the ''Zephyr One'', which they use to escape. Using the pod, Fitz is put to sleep for the next 74 years. He is awakened by Enoch, who prepares him for their arrival at the Lighthouse.
| LineColor       = 322D39
}}
{{Episode list/sublist|Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D. season 5
| EpisodeNumber   = 94
| EpisodeNumber2  = 6
| Title           = Fun & Games
| DirectedBy      = [[Clark Gregg]]
| WrittenBy       = [[Brent Fletcher]]
| OriginalAirDate = {{Start date|2018|1|5}}
| Viewers         = 2.49<ref name="506Ratings">{{Cite web |last=Porter |first=Rick |date=January 8, 2018 |title='Child Support,' 'MacGyver,' everything else steady: Friday final ratings |url=http://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/daily-ratings/friday-final-ratings-jan-5-2018/ |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180108232733/http://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/daily-ratings/friday-final-ratings-jan-5-2018/ |archive-date=January 8, 2018 |access-date=January 8, 2018 |website=[[TV by the Numbers]]}}</ref>
| ShortSummary    = Down in the station, the Kree have harvested some of the youth for an unscheduled terrigenesis ceremony. [[Flint (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Flint]], a friend of Tess, experiences a successful terrigenesis and is taken into hiding with the team by Yo-Yo. Tess is hanged for Flint's disappearance. During a dinner with the other bidders, Fitz quickly proves himself a formidable character, earning Kasius' respect. The first exhibition is then held between Ben and May, resulting in May being sent to the surface while Ben is killed for lying during Daisy's interrogation. Meanwhile, Grill finds the team and holds them captive until Flint saves them, killing Grill with geokinesis. The unexpected arrival of Kasius' brother prompts Sinara to battle Daisy as her exhibition, during which Daisy, Fitz, and Simmons are able to subdue the others and escape. During the escape, Simmons proposes to Fitz.
| LineColor       = 322D39
}}
{{Episode list/sublist|Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D. season 5
| EpisodeNumber   = 95
| EpisodeNumber2  = 7
| Title           = Together or Not at All
| DirectedBy      = [[Brad Turner (director)|Brad Turner]]
| WrittenBy       = Matt Owens
| OriginalAirDate = {{Start date|2018|1|12}}
| Viewers         = 2.31<ref name="507Ratings">{{Cite web |last=Porter |first=Rick |date=January 16, 2018 |title='Hawaii Five-0' adjusts up: Friday final ratings |url=http://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/daily-ratings/friday-final-ratings-jan-12-2018/ |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180117010241/http://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/daily-ratings/friday-final-ratings-jan-12-2018/ |archive-date=January 17, 2018 |access-date=January 16, 2018 |website=[[TV by the Numbers]]}}</ref>
| ShortSummary    = On the surface, Enoch finds May, but their meeting is cut short by an approaching gravity storm. A mysterious figure captures them. Daisy, Fitz, and Simmons are hunted throughout the station and discover the station is being sustained by gravitonium. Fitz is shot during the chase. Deke finds them and takes them to the rest of the team. Reunited, the team plots their escape to the Earth's surface by using a trawler and Deke's anti-gravity device. After learning about Tess' death, Flint decides to stay on the station to protect the remaining inhabitants. Mack and Yo-Yo agree to stay behind and help him. Coulson, Daisy, Fitz, Simmons, and Deke fly to the surface, but get caught in the gravity storm. Meanwhile, Kasius kills his brother and plots to regain his father's acceptance by recapturing Daisy with help from Sinara. On the surface, the mysterious figure takes Enoch and May to safety, where they are greeted by an elderly Robin.
| LineColor       = 322D39
}}
{{Episode list/sublist|Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D. season 5
| EpisodeNumber   = 96
| EpisodeNumber2  = 8
| Title           = The Last Day
| DirectedBy      = Nina Lopez-Corrado
| WrittenBy       = James C. Oliver & Sharla Oliver
| OriginalAirDate = {{Start date|2018|1|19}}
| Viewers         = 2.41<ref name="508Ratings">{{Cite web |last=Porter |first=Rick |date=January 22, 2018 |title='Penn & Teller: Fool Us' rerun adjusts down: Friday final ratings |url=http://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/daily-ratings/friday-final-ratings-jan-19-2018/ |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180123022530/http://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/daily-ratings/friday-final-ratings-jan-19-2018/ |archive-date=January 23, 2018 |access-date=January 23, 2018 |website=[[TV by the Numbers]]}}</ref>
| ShortSummary    = Coulson, Daisy, Fitz, Simmons, and Deke survive the crash and reunite with May in the ''Zephyr''. They meet [[Samuel Voss]], an acquaintance of Deke's father. Up on the Lighthouse, Kasius punishes the inhabitants by cutting off their resources. Flint, Mack, and Yo-Yo go to retrieve the weapons hidden by Fitz and discover Kasius has released the [[Vrellnexians (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Vrellnexians]] onto the lower levels. They defeat the Vrellnexians and rescue the remaining inhabitants. On the surface, the team struggles to get answers from Robin and finds a machine built into the ''Zephyr''. While Fitz and Simmons attempt to remove Daisy's inhibitor, May and Coulson find a shard of the time monolith in Voss' locker. Deke questions Voss about the shard, which belonged to his parents, and gets knocked out. Voss then tries to kill Daisy and impales Robin to prevent her from giving the team answers. Before dying, Robin is comforted by May as she reveals their history and finally tells May how to save the world, a method that will require Flint. In the past, May is shown taking care of Robin and encouraging Fitz to build his machine so they can travel through time.
| LineColor       = 322D39
}}
{{Episode list/sublist|Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D. season 5
| EpisodeNumber   = 97
| EpisodeNumber2  = 9
| Title           = Best Laid Plans
| DirectedBy      = [[Garry A. Brown (producer)|Garry A. Brown]]
| WrittenBy       = George Kitson
| OriginalAirDate = {{Start date|2018|1|26}}
| Viewers         = 2.27<ref name="509Ratings">{{Cite web |last=Porter |first=Rick |date=January 29, 2018 |title='Blindspot,' 'Agents of SHIELD,' all others hold: Friday final ratings |url=http://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/daily-ratings/friday-final-ratings-jan-26-2018/ |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180130004117/http://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/daily-ratings/friday-final-ratings-jan-26-2018/ |archive-date=January 30, 2018 |access-date=January 29, 2018 |website=[[TV by the Numbers]]}}</ref>
| ShortSummary    = As the gravity storm worsens, the team attempts to relaunch the ''Zephyr''. May reveals that, using the shard, Flint can recreate the monolith, allowing the team to travel back through time. Similar to the Lighthouse, Fitz and Simmons find gravitonium on the ''Zephyr'' and realize the designs were manufactured by Fitz himself. On the station, Flint, Mack, and Yo-Yo successfully gain control of the lower levels. Tess is resurrected by Kasius and sent to relay his demands, threatening to kill everyone by detonating explosives if they are not met. Mack and Yo-Yo retaliate by placing the explosives on Level 35, the medical floor, which would prevent Kasius from breeding more Inhumans. During a standoff with Kasius, Flint evacuates the inhabitants to the upper levels and uses the remaining explosives to separate them from the lower levels, out of Kasius' reach. Using the gravity storm to her advantage, May navigates the ''Zephyr'' into space as Daisy battles Sinara again, this time killing her. Daisy then contacts Mack while the team heads for the Lighthouse. Kasius reveals he has his own seer telling him what will happen.
| LineColor       = 322D39
}}
{{Episode list/sublist|Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D. season 5
| EpisodeNumber   = 98
| EpisodeNumber2  = 10
| Title           = Past Life
| DirectedBy      = [[Eric Laneuville]]
| WrittenBy       = DJ Doyle
| OriginalAirDate = {{Start date|2018|2|2}}
| Viewers         = 2.22<ref name="510Ratings">{{Cite web |last=Porter |first=Rick |date=February 5, 2018 |title='Hell's Kitchen' finale, 'Jane the Virgin,' all others hold: Friday final ratings |url=http://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/daily-ratings/friday-final-ratings-feb-2-2018/ |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180206131453/http://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/daily-ratings/friday-final-ratings-feb-2-2018/ |archive-date=February 6, 2018 |access-date=February 5, 2018 |website=[[TV by the Numbers]]}}</ref>
| ShortSummary    = While Enoch stays on the ''Zephyr'', the team focuses on getting to Flint and rescuing the other Inhumans from captivity. Distraught over Sinara's death, Kasius infects Tye, the Inhuman trainer, with odium, a substance that excites maniacal behavior, and sends him after the team. During a fight with Tye, Coulson seemingly gets infected. Kasius' seer is revealed to be Yo-Yo from the future, one who has lived through the time loop and endured endless torture. She reveals that the team's ultimate return will bring about the end of the world and that the only solution is to let Coulson succumb to his infection. As Flint recreates the monolith, Mack leaves to find Yo-Yo and witnesses her future self's death by Kasius, who consumes the remaining odium and fights him. With help from Simmons, Mack kills Kasius and reunites with Yo-Yo, who is still alive in their timeline. Deke returns to the ''Zephyr'' in time to save Enoch and fix the machine, although seemingly at the cost of both of their lives, as the team returns to the present.
| LineColor       = 322D39
}}
{{Episode list/sublist|Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D. season 5
| EpisodeNumber   = 99
| EpisodeNumber2  = 11
| Title           = All the Comforts of Home
| DirectedBy      = [[Kate Woods]]
| WrittenBy       = Drew Z. Greenberg
| OriginalAirDate = {{Start date|2018|3|2}}
| Viewers         = 1.90<ref name="511Ratings">{{Cite web |last=Porter |first=Rick |date=March 5, 2018 |title='Blue Bloods,' 'Blindspot,' all others unchanged: Friday final ratings |url=http://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/daily-ratings/friday-final-ratings-march-2-2018/ |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180309155429/http://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/daily-ratings/friday-final-ratings-march-2-2018/ |archive-date=March 9, 2018 |access-date=March 5, 2018 |website=[[TV by the Numbers]]}}</ref>
| ShortSummary    = Back in their time, the team meets [[Noah (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Noah]], Enoch's successor, who has been monitoring the world from the Lighthouse in their absence. Coulson, May, Fitz, Simmons, Mack, and Yo-Yo investigate a beacon emitting from Earth that fits Voss' description of the first signs of the end. Reluctant to join the team, Daisy stays behind and discovers that Deke survived the explosion. After he is arrested, Daisy is forced to leave the bunker to save him and prevent him from exposing the team, who are now [[Most wanted list|most wanted]]. Upon finding the beacon, the team reunites with Agent [[Piper (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Piper]], who is revealed to be working for General Hale. They are then ambushed by a group of Hale's robotic soldiers, led by an assassin. During the fight, the assassin attempts to kill Mack with their [[chakram]], but Yo-Yo blocks the attack and loses both her arms. Piper realigns with the team as they retreat to the Lighthouse with the beacon, which detonates as Noah sacrifices himself to save Daisy and Fitz. Later, General Hale criticizes the assassin, revealed to be her daughter, [[Ruby Hale|Ruby]], for jeopardizing the operation. In [[Philadelphia]], General Hale recruits [[Carl Creel (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Carl Creel]] to join her team and he reluctantly agrees.
| LineColor       = 322D39
}}
{{Episode list/sublist|Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D. season 5
| EpisodeNumber   = 100
| EpisodeNumber2  = 12
| Title           = [[The Real Deal (Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D.)|The Real Deal]]
| DirectedBy      = [[Kevin Tancharoen]]
| WrittenBy       = Jed Whedon & Maurissa Tancharoen & [[Jeffrey Bell]]
| OriginalAirDate = {{Start date|2018|3|9}}
| Viewers         = 2.04<ref name="512Ratings">{{Cite web |last=Porter |first=Rick |date=March 12, 2018 |title='Blue Bloods,' 'Taken,' 'Confronting Putin' adjust down: Friday final ratings |url=http://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/daily-ratings/friday-final-ratings-march-9-2018/ |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180313031740/http://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/daily-ratings/friday-final-ratings-march-9-2018/ |archive-date=March 13, 2018 |access-date=March 12, 2018 |website=[[TV by the Numbers]]}}</ref>
| ShortSummary    = The beacon's explosion destroys three monoliths that were being stored in the bunker, creating a dimensional rift that manifests the fears of the team. Using [[gravitonium]], Fitz creates a device capable of sealing the rift; Coulson volunteers to deliver the device, but then collapses. The team finds out about his infection, a result of the [[Robbie Reyes (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Ghost Rider]] burning off the life-sustaining GH-325 drug within him. The team is forced to accelerate their plan when Yo-Yo is attacked by the manifestation of a Simmons [[Life Model Decoy (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Life Model Decoy]] (LMD). Coulson sends Deke to the surface to call for backup, then proceeds alone to seal the rift. He encounters a manifestation of [[Mike Peterson (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Mike Peterson]], who claims that Coulson's experiences are just a dream and that he is dying on an operating table after the [[Battle of New York (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Battle of New York]]. Coulson overcomes his fear and is saved by the real Peterson, who responds to Deke's call and arrives with several other S.H.I.E.L.D. agents. Coulson and Peterson fight off manifestations of Vrellnexians, [[Lash (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Lash]], and [[Hive (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Hive]] before managing to contain the rift. Later, the team organizes a wedding ceremony for Fitz and Simmons. General Hale, who is investigating sightings of Daisy, finds evidence that Deke is related to Fitz and Simmons.
| LineColor       = 322D39
}}
{{Episode list/sublist|Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D. season 5
| EpisodeNumber   = 101
| EpisodeNumber2  = 13
| Title           = Principia
| DirectedBy      = Brad Turner
| WrittenBy       = Craig Titley
| OriginalAirDate = {{Start date|2018|3|16}}
| Viewers         = 2.07<ref name="513Ratings">{{Cite web |last=Porter |first=Rick |date=March 19, 2018 |title=NCAA Tournament adjusts down: Friday final ratings |url=http://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/daily-ratings/friday-final-ratings-march-16-2018/ |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180320043704/http://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/daily-ratings/friday-final-ratings-march-16-2018/ |archive-date=March 20, 2018 |access-date=March 19, 2018 |website=[[TV by the Numbers]]}}</ref>
| ShortSummary    = When the rift begins to reopen, Fitz sends the team to search for more gravitonium. The team hunts down a lead in [[Baton Rouge]]; Mack reunites with his school mate, [[Tony Caine (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Tony Caine]], who has been helping to redeem scientists coerced into working for [[Hydra (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Hydra]] through Cybertek Industries. Caine states that the gravitonium was in transport aboard the ''Principia'', a Cybertek ship that went missing. Deke realizes the gravitonium may have been activated by the lightning storm, sending the ''Principia'' into the sky. Following Deke's theory, the team finds the ''Principia'' suspended in the atmosphere and discovers most of the gravitonium is gone, leaving only a small portion to sustain the ship. As Mack collects the remaining gravitonium, a group of Hale's robotic soldiers ambushes them. The team successfully escapes the ship before it plummets back to Earth. Upon hearing his mother's saying in an exchange between Simmons and Yo-Yo, Deke realizes Fitz and Simmons are his grandparents. Meanwhile, General Hale continues to form her team by attempting to recruit [[Werner von Strucker (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Werner von Strucker]], whose memory was enhanced after S.H.I.E.L.D. revived him from a vegetative state.{{efn|As depicted in "[[Bouncing Back]]".}} While Strucker initially rejects Hale's offer, Ruby convinces him to stay.
| LineColor       = 322D39
}}
{{Episode list/sublist|Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D. season 5
| EpisodeNumber   = 102
